You are coordinating a smart farm and must manage a drone fleet that protects crops from birds. The main objective is to minimize crop damage across every field.

At the start, birds move around the farm randomly. At times they decide to feed, choose a target field, and fly toward it. Their preference over fields changes over time, and they are also more attracted to fields where more birds are already present. After a bird lands in a field, it waits for a fixed period before causing damage. Once damage is dealt, the bird either attacks another crop in the same field or leaves the area.

Every field has sensors that detect bird presence. A field with more birds reports a higher threat level.

